1
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:05,980
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 11=

2
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:07,720
The criminal, Wang Wen,

3
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:08,960
has committed heinous crimes

4
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:10,120
that violate all reason.

5
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,120
He is sentenced to 60 lashes.

6
00:01:12,550 --> 00:01:14,000
The system of pawning wives

7
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:15,310
violates the laws of nature above

8
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,510
and human morality below.

9
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:19,600
It goes against
the principles of the sages

10
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,960
and is incompatible
with governing by benevolence.

11
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:25,360
From the day this decree is issued,

12
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,680
the corrupt custom of pawning wives

13
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:28,120
shall be abolished immediately.

14
00:01:28,680 --> 00:01:31,040
Anyone who dares to pawn
or sell their wives again,

15
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,680
be it the original husband

16
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:33,680
or the pawnbroker,

17
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,600
shall be severely punished
according to the law.

18
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,560
Local officials must perform
their duties faithfully

19
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:42,120
and strictly investigate
such lawbreakers.

20
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,200
Those who shield or tolerate them

21
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,880
shall be punished alongside them.

22
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,840
By Imperial Decree.

23
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:15,540
(Anping Bridge)

24
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:36,620
(Anping Bridge)

25
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,200
(There are countless
injustices in this world.)

26
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:41,400
(What good does it do
to seek justice for others?)

27
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,360
(Change...)

28
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,840
(Changing these unjust laws)

29
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,440
(is the only way forward.)

30
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:48,960
Your Highness,

31
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,520
Advocate Jiang Xiaobai
requests an audience.

32
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,840
Advocate Jiang, for what purpose

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,160
have you entered the palace today?

34
00:02:55,390 --> 00:02:56,700
To revise the laws of Bojue.

35
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,570
It's a beautiful day.

36
00:02:59,830 --> 00:03:00,800
Walk with me.

37
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,080
All right.

38
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:09,080
That day at the joint trial,

39
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,360
I heard your impassioned speech

40
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:12,880
clearly.

41
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,880
You have a unique insight

42
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,200
into the law,

43
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,720
and the knowledge of law
you demonstrated

44
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,960
earned my deep admiration.

45
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,360
You flatter me, Your Highness.

46
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,080
I just couldn't stand
seeing such injustice.

47
00:03:26,750 --> 00:03:27,600
Relying on the little legal knowledge

48
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,040
I usually study,

49
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:31,160
I simply plucked up the courage

50
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:32,920
to speak my mind.

51
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:34,640
Don't be overly modest.

52
00:03:35,040 --> 00:03:36,080
I know very well

53
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,440
that the Bojue Kingdom

54
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,200
has many shortcomings in its laws.

55
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,880
And these shortcomings

56
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:45,200
often give those with ill intentions

57
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:46,800
loopholes to exploit.

58
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,080
Take the wife-pawning case for instance.

59
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,440
It was clearly an atrocious act,

60
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,880
yet it almost went unpunished

61
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,240
due to unclear laws.

62
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,400
Revising the laws

63
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,960
is a matter of great importance,

64
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,120
and the process

65
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:02,240
will surely bring many difficulties.

66
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:05,120
If you encounter any trouble,

67
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,520
just tell me.

68
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,720
I will fully support you.

69
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:11,680
Once the laws

70
00:04:11,840 --> 00:04:13,400
are fully revised,

71
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,160
the Bojue Kingdom

72
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,400
will surely see far fewer injustices.

73
00:04:18,120 --> 00:04:18,720
The people

74
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,200
can also live and work in peace.

75
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:22,640
What you're doing

76
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:24,600
will benefit generations to come.

77
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,440
You praise me too much, Your Highness.

78
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:28,600
I only

79
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,880
hope to do my modest best

80
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:32,440
to bring a little less suffering

81
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:33,760
and a little more fairness

82
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:34,680
to this world,

83
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,760
then it will all be worth it.

84
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,320
I'll burn you to death,
you wretched woman.

85
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:05,400
Xiaobai.

86
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:32,080
If two people's heartlines

87
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,840
can connect like this,

88
00:06:33,840 --> 00:06:36,240
it means they're a match made in heaven.

89
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,080
What are you trying to do?

90
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:12,070
♪The feelings
I secretly hid for so long♪

91
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:15,430
♪My heart gently stirs as you draw near♪

92
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:19,110
♪The starry sky I once gazed upon♪

93
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:19,920
What do you want?

94
00:07:19,930 --> 00:07:22,260
♪Now falls into my eyes♪

95
00:07:23,060 --> 00:07:26,160
♪The evening breeze softly
stirs my heartbeat♪

96
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:29,180
♪Even the silence feels so tender♪

97
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,770
♪I've imagined
our meeting countless times♪

98
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:35,580
♪Yet this moment
feels more vivid than a dream♪

99
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:38,040
♪When you take my hand♪

100
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,930
♪Fireworks bloom across the night sky♪

101
00:07:39,930 --> 00:07:41,580
♪Every other sight fades away♪

102
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,400
♪Leaving only your eyes♪

103
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:45,080
♪Moonlight falls upon my shoulder♪

104
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,760
♪Happiness quietly finds its voice♪

105
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:48,680
♪The sweetest kind of tenderness♪

106
00:07:48,690 --> 00:07:50,420
♪Is simply being here with you♪

107
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:52,110
♪When you hold my hand tight♪

108
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:53,990
♪Starlight spills across the branches♪

109
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,760
♪The years drift slowly by♪

110
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:57,340
♪Warmth fills my heart♪

111
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:59,230
♪The evening breeze kisses my brow♪

112
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:01,060
♪Beautiful moments slowly come together♪

113
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,040
♪Along the long road that lies ahead♪

114
00:08:03,050 --> 00:08:05,010
♪May I stay by your side♪

115
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:22,460
♪Walking together
through the lit streets♪

116
00:08:22,900 --> 00:08:25,990
♪Every step falls on a heartbeat♪

117
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:29,820
♪The warmth of your palm is so deep♪

118
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:33,230
♪Taking away all my uneasiness♪

119
00:08:33,690 --> 00:08:36,700
♪Waiting without needing another word♪

120
00:08:37,070 --> 00:08:40,050
♪The answer has long
lingered in your smile♪

121
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:42,890
♪A tacit response from heart to heart♪

122
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,000
Your injury...

123
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:46,320
It's nothing.

124
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,690
♪When you take my hand♪

125
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:50,550
♪Fireworks bloom across the night sky♪

126
00:08:50,580 --> 00:08:52,290
♪Every other sight fades away♪

127
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:54,010
♪Leaving only your eyes♪

128
00:08:54,010 --> 00:08:55,800
♪Moonlight falls upon my shoulder♪

129
00:08:57,040 --> 00:08:58,000
Your Highness,

130
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,920
has Sihzou's health improved at all?

131
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,440
He is fine now.

132
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,600
I apologize for coming unannounced.

133
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:06,040
There's something
I'd like to discuss with you.

134
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,680
Please go ahead, Prince Luan.

135
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:10,320
My niece, Rousang,

136
00:09:10,560 --> 00:09:12,640
has now reached the age for marriage.

137
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,400
Sizhou, the First Prince,

138
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:15,600
possesses fine character and looks

139
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:16,840
and is kind and generous.

140
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,080
I wonder if

141
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:20,080
Rousang could be

142
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,600
betrothed to the First Prince.

143
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,360
Sizhou

144
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,480
has indeed reached marriageable age,

145
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:27,760
but

146
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,240
marriage is a major matter.

147
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,480
Shouldn't we also ask

148
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,080
for the young ones' opinions?

149
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:33,400
Can something as important as marriage

150
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,160
really be left to the young ones?

151
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,960
Since ancient times,

152
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,120
it has always been the elders
who make the decisions.

153
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:42,000
As the patriarch and parents,

154
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,680
of course we must
plan thoroughly for them.

155
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:50,120
Now that His Majesty
is bedridden with illness,

156
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:52,680
many matters
inside and outside the court

157
00:09:52,880 --> 00:09:54,840
do indeed require extra support.

158
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:56,720
It's just that I wonder if they...

159
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:57,680
Rest assured, Your Highness.

160
00:09:58,160 --> 00:09:59,480
Rousang

161
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,640
is obedient and sensible.

162
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,480
I am certain

163
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:04,800
she will get along harmoniously
with the First Prince.

164
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:05,760
Besides,

165
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,400
with our backing,

166
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:09,160
the First Prince's

167
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:11,200
future endeavors

168
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,880
will proceed even more smoothly.

169
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,560
Whether for the public good
or private interest,

170
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,880
it is a wonderful match.

171
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:19,120
(Prince Luan holds great power.)

172
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:21,360
(If we form an alliance
through Rousang,)

173
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,800
(it could serve as support
for Sizhou's succession to the throne.)

174
00:10:28,240 --> 00:10:29,960
Since you put it that way,

175
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,160
we shall do as you say.

176
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:36,000
I only hope that in the future,
these two children

177
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,440
can live peacefully together.

178
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:39,960
Your Highness is wise.

179
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,720
I shall return and make
the arrangements right away.

180
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,760
I will ensure this wedding

181
00:10:44,040 --> 00:10:45,400
is handled grandly.

182
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,440
(To achieve supreme power,)

183
00:10:55,040 --> 00:10:56,240
(one must break the old order
to establish the new.)

184
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:59,320
(Decisions must be made
without hesitation.)

185
00:11:05,550 --> 00:11:08,150
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

186
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:11,510
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

187
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:13,910
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

188
00:11:13,910 --> 00:11:16,830
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

189
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:21,710
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

190
00:11:22,070 --> 00:11:25,390
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

191
00:11:25,990 --> 00:11:27,550
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

192
00:11:27,710 --> 00:11:31,030
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

193
00:11:33,790 --> 00:11:36,670
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

194
00:11:37,190 --> 00:11:40,270
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

195
00:11:40,710 --> 00:11:43,310
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

196
00:11:43,310 --> 00:11:47,350
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

197
00:11:47,590 --> 00:11:50,630
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

198
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:53,710
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

199
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:56,430
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

200
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:59,670
♪I'll only say that once♪

201
00:12:00,150 --> 00:12:01,910
♪I called your name♪

202
00:12:06,510 --> 00:12:08,750
♪The silent stars hang low♪

203
00:12:10,150 --> 00:12:12,350
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

204
00:12:13,590 --> 00:12:15,510
♪I linger in the old tower♪

205
00:12:15,630 --> 00:12:19,270
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

206
00:12:20,590 --> 00:12:23,030
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

207
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,710
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

208
00:12:27,470 --> 00:12:29,710
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

209
00:12:29,710 --> 00:12:35,950
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

210
00:12:36,230 --> 00:12:39,110
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

211
00:12:39,710 --> 00:12:43,190
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

212
00:12:43,190 --> 00:12:45,830
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

213
00:12:45,830 --> 00:12:50,110
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

214
00:12:50,110 --> 00:12:53,030
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

215
00:12:53,470 --> 00:12:56,190
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

216
00:12:56,190 --> 00:12:58,870
♪If we meet again in another life♪

217
00:12:59,190 --> 00:13:01,910
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

218
00:13:02,590 --> 00:13:04,870
♪Was when we first met?♪

219
00:13:06,150 --> 00:13:08,550
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

220
00:13:09,670 --> 00:13:11,430
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
